    "note": "EC given in mS/cm as published; ppm500 = EC_mS_per_cm * 500, computed here for direct comparison against the Grove TDS sensor's native 500-scale output.",
    "ph_tolerance_note": "ph_min/ph_max are the published optimum ranges (setpoint is taken from their overlap). ph_tolerance_min/ph_tolerance_max are the wider range the plant grows normally in, used as the controller dead limits: the optimum +/- 0.5 pH, clipped to 5.0-7.5. Plants shift pH themselves as they take up ions, so pH is only corrected when it leaves this range. Most hydroponic crops are grown at pH 5.5-6.5; above about 6.5 iron, manganese and phosphorus availability falls, and below about 5.5 calcium and magnesium uptake falls."
